{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '95,155p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/artifact_ref.go; sed -n '1,235p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/roots.go; sed -n '620,735p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; rg -n 'func gitOutputIn|checkIndexInputs|inputBinding|Audit|Closure' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; cat .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md\"","aggregated_output":"type ArtifactResolver struct {\n\tRoots *Roots\n\t// Authorize runs BEFORE registry lookup, including for transitive refs.\n\t// nil is the trusted local CLI boundary: explicitly configured roots only.\n\tAuthorize func(projectID string) bool\n\t// snapshots, when set, gives every store this resolver opens one spec\n\t// listing per project for the operation (spec\n\t// pose-attention-within-a-second).\n\tsnapshots *sync.Map\n\t// FS is the filesystem of the operation the resolver serves; every store\n\t// it opens carries it (spec pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update D2).\n\tFS Files\n\n\t// Governance bounds project crossings in dependency graphs, and separately\n\t// bounds authority-transfer redirect chains (legacy redirect depth is 16).\n\tgovernanceDepthLimit int\n}\n\nfunc (r ArtifactResolver) fsys() Files { return FilesOrNative(r.FS) }\n\n// WithSpecSnapshots returns a resolver whose stores read each project's specs\n// once for the rest of the operation.\nfunc (r ArtifactResolver) WithSpecSnapshots() ArtifactResolver {\n\tr.snapshots = &sync.Map{}\n\treturn r\n}\n\n// withSpecSnapshot gives a store the operation's one spec listing of its project, when the\n// resolver carries snapshots; without them the store is returned as it is.\nfunc (r ArtifactResolver) withSpecSnapshot(project string, s Store) Store {\n\tif r.snapshots != nil {\n\t\tsnapshot, _ := r.snapshots.LoadOrStore(project, &specSnapshot{})\n\t\ts.specs = snapshot.(*specSnapshot)\n\t}\n\treturn s\n}\n\nfunc (r ArtifactResolver) Resolve(localProject, raw string) ArtifactResolution {\n\treturn r.resolve(localProject, raw, map[string]bool{}, 0)\n}\n\nfunc (r ArtifactResolver) resolve(localProject, raw string, redirectPath map[string]bool, redirectDepth int) ArtifactResolution {\n\tout := ArtifactResolution{SchemaVersion: 1}\n\tref, err := ParseArtifactRef(raw)\n\tif err != nil || !filepath.IsLocal(ref.Slug) {\n\t\tout.State = \"invalid-artifact-reference\"\n\t\treturn out\n\t}\n\tif ref.Project == \"\" {\n\t\tref.Project = localProject\n\t}\n\tout.Identity = ref\n\tif r.Authorize != nil && !r.Authorize(ref.Project) {\n\t\tout.State = \"unauthorized-project\"\n\t\treturn out\n\t}\n\tif r.Roots == nil {\n\t\tout.State = \"unknown-project\"\n\t\treturn out\n\t}\n\ts, err := r.Roots.StoreFor(ref.Project)\npackage pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"slices\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// RootsConfig configures project_id -> root resolution (pose-mcp-multi-project,\n// pose-mcp-runtime-refresh).\ntype RootsConfig struct {\n\tDefaultRoot      string            // root for empty project_id (legacy single-root)\n\tDefaultProjectID string            // also mapped to DefaultRoot when non-empty\n\tProjectsDir      string            // base scanned for materialized projects\n\tProjectIDPrefix  string            // dirname -> prefix+dirname (default \"\": dirname IS the project_id)\n\tExplicit         map[string]string // env override, wins over scan/default\n\t// StrictSelection (spec pose-mcp-project-scope-contract): when true, an\n\t// empty project_id in a deployment that has onboarded more than one\n\t// project fails closed with ProjectAmbiguousError instead of silently\n\t// resolving to DefaultRoot. Default false preserves existing\n\t// single-project stdio ergonomics and gives multi-project deployments an\n\t// announced deprecation window before this becomes the default.\n\tStrictSelection bool\n}\n\n// ProjectUnknownError means project_id was provided but does not resolve to\n// any registered root, even after a rescan. It never carries a filesystem\n// path — only the caller-supplied logical identifier.\ntype ProjectUnknownError struct{ ProjectID string }\n\nfunc (e ProjectUnknownError) Error() string {\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"unknown project_id %q\", e.ProjectID)\n}\n\n// ProjectAmbiguousError means project_id was omitted and the server cannot\n// (or, in strict mode, will not) pick one root unambiguously.\n//\n//   - \"no-default\": no default root is configured at all.\n//   - \"multi-project-implicit\": a default root is configured but more than\n//     one project is registered, so omitting project_id is a deprecated,\n//     strict-mode-rejectable convenience rather than a real single-project\n//     deployment.\ntype ProjectAmbiguousError struct{ Reason string }\n\nfunc (e ProjectAmbiguousError) Error() string {\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"ambiguous project selection: %s (pass project_id explicitly)\", e.Reason)\n}\n\n// Roots resolves a project_id to a project-scoped Store. The registry is rebuilt\n// from the projects dir on demand: a project cloned at runtime resolves on the\n// next miss (rescan), so freshly onboarded repos appear without a restart.\ntype Roots struct {\n\tcfg       RootsConfig\n\tmu        sync.RWMutex\n\tbyProject map[string]string\n\tconflicts map[string]bool\n\t// governanceStores is an operation-local overlay used when a multi-root\n\t// writer has already authorized and guarded its complete root set.\n\tgovernanceStores map[string]Store\n\tlastScan         time.Time\n\trescanWindow     time.Duration\n\t// fs is the filesystem of the operation the registry serves; the stores\n\t// it hands out carry it.\n\tfs Files\n}\n\nfunc (r *Roots) fsys() Files { return FilesOrNative(r.fs) }\n\nfunc (r *Roots) storeFor(projectID, root string) Store {\n\tfiles := r.fsys()\n\tif view, carrier := governanceReadViewFromFiles(files); view != nil && carrier != nil {\n\t\tif projectID == \"\" {\n\t\t\tprojectID = r.cfg.DefaultProjectID\n\t\t}\n\t\tfiles = view.filesForProject(carrier.producer, projectID)\n\t}\n\treturn Store{Root: root, FS: files}\n}\n\n// RootsContext is the path-free runtime view exposed to MCP diagnostics. It\n// deliberately contains only logical identifiers and selection behavior; the\n// project_id -> filesystem-root map remains private to Roots.\ntype RootsContext struct {\n\tDefaultProjectID  string    `json:\"default_project_id,omitempty\"`\n\tDefaultConfigured bool      `json:\"default_configured\"`\n\tStrictSelection   bool      `json:\"strict_project_selection\"`\n\tProjectIDs        []string  `json:\"project_ids\"`\n\tRefreshedAt       time.Time `json:\"refreshed_at\"`\n}\n\n// NewRoots builds and primes the registry.\nfunc NewRootsIn(files Files, cfg RootsConfig) *Roots {\n\tr := &Roots{cfg: cfg, rescanWindow: 2 * time.Second, fs: files}\n\tr.rebuild()\n\treturn r\n}\n\n// NewRoots reads and writes the filesystem directly; NewRootsIn takes the\n// operation's files.\nfunc NewRoots(cfg RootsConfig) *Roots {\n\treturn NewRootsIn(NativeFiles(), cfg)\n}\n\nfunc (r *Roots) rebuild() {\n\tm := map[string]string{}\n\tconflicts := map[string]bool{}\n\tif r.cfg.DefaultProjectID != \"\" && r.cfg.DefaultRoot != \"\" {\n\t\tm[r.cfg.DefaultProjectID] = r.cfg.DefaultRoot\n\t}\n\tif scan, err := ScanProjectsDirIn(r.fsys(), r.cfg.ProjectsDir, r.cfg.ProjectIDPrefix); err == nil {\n\t\tfor k, v := range scan {\n\t\t\tif previous, ok := m[k]; ok && !sameProjectRoot(r.fsys(), previous, v) {\n\t\t\t\tconflicts[k] = true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tm[k] = v\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor k, v := range r.cfg.Explicit {\n\t\tif k != \"\" && v != \"\" {\n\t\t\tm[k] = v\n\t\t\tdelete(conflicts, k)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tr.mu.Lock()\n\tr.byProject = m\n\tr.conflicts = conflicts\n\tr.lastScan = time.Now()\n\tr.mu.Unlock()\n}\n\n// maybeRescan rebuilds the registry if the throttle window has elapsed, so a\n// stream of misses for an unknown id does not trigger a readdir storm.\nfunc (r *Roots) maybeRescan() {\n\tr.mu.RLock()\n\tstale := time.Since(r.lastScan) >= r.rescanWindow\n\tr.mu.RUnlock()\n\tif stale {\n\t\tr.rebuild()\n\t}\n}\n\n// StoreFor resolves the Store for a project_id. Empty -> default root (or a\n// distinct ProjectAmbiguousError when no default is configured, or, under\n// StrictSelection, when more than one project is registered). Known\n// project_id -> its root. An unknown id triggers one throttled rescan (a\n// project may have just been cloned) before returning ProjectUnknownError;\n// there is no silent fallback.\nfunc (r *Roots) StoreFor(projectID string) (Store, error) {\n\tr.mu.RLock()\n\tguarded, hasGuarded := r.governanceStores[projectID]\n\tr.mu.RUnlock()\n\tif hasGuarded {\n\t\treturn guarded, nil\n\t}\n\tif projectID == \"\" {\n\t\tif r.cfg.DefaultRoot == \"\" {\n\t\t\treturn Store{}, ProjectAmbiguousError{Reason: \"no-default\"}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif r.cfg.StrictSelection && r.registeredProjectCount() > 1 {\n\t\t\treturn Store{}, ProjectAmbiguousError{Reason: \"multi-project-implicit\"}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn r.storeFor(r.cfg.DefaultProjectID, r.cfg.DefaultRoot), nil\n\t}\n\tr.mu.RLock()\n\troot, ok := r.byProject[projectID]\n\tconflict := r.conflicts[projectID]\n\tr.mu.RUnlock()\n\tif conflict {\n\t\treturn Store{}, ProjectBindingConflictError{ProjectID: projectID}\n\t}\n\tif !ok {\n\t\tr.maybeRescan()\n\t\tr.mu.RLock()\n\t\troot, ok = r.byProject[projectID]\n\t\tconflict = r.conflicts[projectID]\n\t\tr.mu.RUnlock()\n\t\tif conflict {\n\t\t\treturn Store{}, ProjectBindingConflictError{ProjectID: projectID}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif !ok {\n\t\treturn Store{}, ProjectUnknownError{ProjectID: projectID}\n\t}\n\treturn r.storeFor(projectID, root), nil\n}\n\nfunc (r *Roots) registeredProjectCount() int {\n\tr.mu.RLock()\n\tdefer r.mu.RUnlock()\n\treturn len(r.byProject)\n}\n\n// Refresh forces an immediate rebuild of the registry, bypassing the rescan\n// throttle (portal-workspace-scale: an explicit, authenticated push signal from\n// the Conductor after onboarding, not a passive on-miss rescan).\nfunc (r *Roots) Refresh() {\n\tr.rebuild()\n}\n\n// Projects returns the currently known project_ids (for diagnostics/logging).\nfunc (r *Roots) Projects() []string {\n\treturn r.Context().ProjectIDs\n}\n\n// Context returns a deterministic, path-free snapshot of the active registry.\n// It is safe for diagnostics but still requires caller authorization before\n// any ProjectIDs are returned over a transport.\nfunc (r *Roots) Context() RootsContext {\n\tr.mu.RLock()\n\tdefer r.mu.RUnlock()\n\tids := make([]string, 0, len(r.byProject))\n\tfor id := range r.byProject {\n\t\tids = append(ids, id)\n\t}\n\tslices.Sort(ids)\n\treturn RootsContext{\n\t\tDefaultProjectID:  r.cfg.DefaultProjectID,\n\t\tDefaultConfigured: r.cfg.DefaultRoot != \"\",\n\t\tStrictSelection:   r.cfg.StrictSelection,\n\t\tProjectIDs:        ids,\n\t\tRefreshedAt:       r.lastScan,\n\t}\n}\n\n// ScanProjectsDir registers each immediate subdirectory of base that contains a\n// .pose/ directory, under the convention project_id = prefix + <dirname>. With an\n// empty prefix the dirname IS the project_id (the canonical onboarding convention:\n// clones land at HARNE8_PROJECTS_DIR/<project_id>).\nfunc ScanProjectsDirIn(files Files, base, projectIDPrefix string) (map[string]string, error) {\n\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) reserveRecord(metadataBytes int64) bool {\n\tif op == nil {\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\top.budgetMu.Lock()\n\tdefer op.budgetMu.Unlock()\n\tif op.records+op.directoryEntries+1 > governanceReadViewMaxRecords || metadataBytes < 0 || metadataBytes > governanceReadViewMaxMetadata-op.metadataBytes {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\top.records++\n\top.metadataBytes += metadataBytes\n\treturn true\n}\n\n// checkIndexInputs verifies the declared source bindings only when a producer\n// actually consumes a derived index. Taking a pin for snapshot identity alone\n// does not make the projection depend on that index, so the projection producer\n// deliberately skips this check. The work is shared per root, generation and\n// producer; each producer still records its own observations and limitation.\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) checkIndexInputs(files Files, root, producer string, pin *IndexGenerationView) []string {\n\tif op == nil || pin == nil || pin.Status != IndexGenerationCurrent {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tif from := op.indexInputsFrom; from != nil && from != op {\n\t\treturn from.checkIndexInputs(op.indexInputsFiles, root, producer, pin)\n\t}\n\tabs, err := filepath.Abs(root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn []string{\"index input root could not be resolved\"}\n\t}\n\tkey := filepath.Clean(abs) + \"\\x00\" + pin.Descriptor.GenerationID + \"\\x00\" + producer\n\top.mu.Lock()\n\tif op.indexInputChecks == nil {\n\t\top.indexInputChecks = map[string]*governanceReadViewIndexInputCheck{}\n\t}\n\tif prior := op.indexInputChecks[key]; prior != nil {\n\t\tready := prior.ready\n\t\top.mu.Unlock()\n\t\t<-ready\n\t\treturn append([]string(nil), prior.reasons...)\n\t}\n\tcheck := &governanceReadViewIndexInputCheck{ready: make(chan struct{})}\n\top.indexInputChecks[key] = check\n\top.mu.Unlock()\n\n\treasons := []string{}\n\tfor _, name := range IndexInputNames {\n\t\tbound, exists := pin.Descriptor.Inputs[name]\n\t\tif !exists || strings.TrimSpace(bound) == \"\" {\n\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"index generation does not bind input \"+name)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tcurrent, known := op.indexInputBinding(files, root, producer, name)\n\t\tif !known || current == \"\" {\n\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"current index input \"+name+\" could not be bounded\")\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif current != bound {\n\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"index input \"+name+\" changed since generation \"+pin.Descriptor.GenerationID)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treasons = uniqueSorted(reasons)\n\top.mu.Lock()\n\tcheck.reasons = append([]string(nil), reasons...)\n\tclose(check.ready)\n\top.mu.Unlock()\n\treturn reasons\n}\n\n// governanceIndexInputBindingObserved sees each computation of an index\n// input's binding; tests count them.\nvar governanceIndexInputBindingObserved = func(root, name string) {}\n\n// Revalidation must use the same captured project/resolver context as the\n// generation consumer, including when that consumer is a foreign Store.\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) indexInputBinding(files Files, root, producer, name string) (string, bool) {\n\tgovernanceIndexInputBindingObserved(root, name)\n\tif name != \"federated-material\" {\n\t\treturn IndexInputBindingIn(files, root, name)\n\t}\n\top.mu.Lock()\n\tproject, selectedRoot := op.rootForPathLocked(governanceAbsoluteRoot(root), \"\")\n\tconflict := op.initialConflicts[project]\n\top.mu.Unlock()\n\tif project == \"\" || conflict || !sameLexicalRoot(root, selectedRoot) {\n\t\treturn \"\", false\n\t}\n\tresolver := op.resolver\n\tresolver.FS = files\n\tresolver.Roots = op.rootsForProducer(resolver.Roots, files, producer)\n\tresolver.snapshots = nil\n\tresolver.governanceDepthLimit = 8\n\treturn IndexInputBindingForStoreIn(Store{Root: root, FS: files, FederatedProjectID: project, FederatedResolver: &resolver}, name)\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) governanceIndexConsumed(status IndexGenerationStatus, err error, pin *IndexGenerationView) {\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tview, carrier := governanceReadViewFromFiles(s.fsys())\n\tif view == nil || carrier == nil || carrier.producer == \"\" || carrier.producer == \"projection\" {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tproducer := carrier.producer\n\tproject := carrier.project\n\tswitch status {\n\tcase IndexGenerationLegacy:\n\t\tmarkGovernanceReadUnknownForProject(s.fsys(), s.Root, project, producer, \"a legacy index has no bound input generation\")\n\t\treturn\n\tcase IndexGenerationCurrent:\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif pin == nil {\n\t\tpin = s.indexPin\n120:\tfinalAudits      map[*governanceReadView]governanceReadViewAudit\n164:type governanceReadViewAudit struct {\n170:type governanceReadViewAuditBudget struct {\n176:func (b *governanceReadViewAuditBudget) reserve(metadata int64) bool {\n185:func (b *governanceReadViewAuditBudget) reserveInput(bytes int64) bool {\n193:func (b *governanceReadViewAuditBudget) reserveDirectory(entries []fs.DirEntry, maxEntries int, maxMetadata int64) bool {\n365:func (op *governanceReadViewOperation) audit() governanceReadViewAudit {\n366:\tresult := governanceReadViewAudit{ChangedProducers: map[string]bool{}, UnknownProducers: map[string][]string{}}\n376:\tperRoot := map[*governanceReadView]governanceReadViewAudit{}\n377:\tauditBudget := &governanceReadViewAuditBudget{}\n395:\t\tgitAudit := op.git.audit()\n396:\t\tprimaryAudit := perRoot[op.primary]\n397:\t\tmergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(&primaryAudit, gitAudit)\n398:\t\tperRoot[op.primary] = primaryAudit\n399:\t\tchanged = append(changed, gitAudit.ChangedPaths...)\n400:\t\tfor producer, value := range gitAudit.ChangedProducers {\n403:\t\tfor producer, reasons := range gitAudit.UnknownProducers {\n410:\t\t\tregistryAudit := governanceReadViewAudit{UnknownProducers: map[string][]string{}}\n415:\t\t\t\tregistryAudit.ChangedPaths = []string{\"authorized-roots\"}\n416:\t\t\t\tregistryAudit.ChangedProducers = map[string]bool{\"projection\": true}\n418:\t\t\tregistryAudit.UnknownProducers[\"projection\"] = []string{reason}\n419:\t\t\tmergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(&result, registryAudit)\n420:\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, registryAudit.ChangedPaths...)\n424:\t\t\tprimaryAudit := perRoot[op.primary]\n425:\t\t\tmergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(&primaryAudit, registryAudit)\n426:\t\t\tperRoot[op.primary] = primaryAudit\n434:\top.finalAudits = perRoot\n439:func mergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(target *governanceReadViewAudit, source governanceReadViewAudit) {\n462:\tfinalAudits := op.finalAudits\n464:\tif finalAudits == nil {\n468:\tfinalAudits = op.finalAudits\n496:\t\taudit := finalAudits[root.view]\n635:// checkIndexInputs verifies the declared source bindings only when a producer\n640:func (op *governanceReadViewOperation) checkIndexInputs(files Files, root, producer string, pin *IndexGenerationView) []string {\n645:\t\treturn from.checkIndexInputs(op.indexInputsFiles, root, producer, pin)\n749:\tfor _, reason := range view.operation.checkIndexInputs(s.fsys(), s.Root, producer, pin) {\n933:\trootMapForAudit := func() (map[string]string, map[string]bool, bool) {\n946:\top.currentRoots = rootMapForAudit\n2077:func (v *governanceReadView) audit() governanceReadViewAudit {\n2084:func (v *governanceReadView) auditSingle() governanceReadViewAudit {\n2085:\treturn v.auditSingleWithBudget(&governanceReadViewAuditBudget{})\n2088:func (v *governanceReadView) auditSingleWithBudget(budget *governanceReadViewAuditBudget) governanceReadViewAudit {\n2115:\tresult := governanceReadViewAudit{ChangedProducers: map[string]bool{}, UnknownProducers: unknown}\n2119:\ttype directoryAudit struct {\n2123:\tdirectories := map[string]directoryAudit{}\n2134:\t\tdirectories[path] = directoryAudit{entries, err}\n2248:func (v *governanceReadView) metadata(project, revision, indexGeneration string, audit governanceReadViewAudit) (ReadViewMetadata, *governanceReadViewProof) {\n2255:func (v *governanceReadView) metadataSingle(project, revision, indexGeneration string, audit governanceReadViewAudit) (ReadViewMetadata, *governanceReadViewProof) {\n# Rule: Knowledge Governance\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when creating, updating, reviewing, or removing artifacts under `.pose/knowledge/`.\n\n## TTL and retention\n\n- Set `expires_at` on every artifact when it is created.\n- Use a default TTL of 30 days for notes, decision logs, and handoffs.\n- Use a TTL of up to 90 days only with a justification recorded in the artifact body.\n- Treat an artifact without `expires_at` as non-compliant and block its creation or merge.\n\n## When this is not the right home\n\n- Use `.pose/knowledge/` only for time-bound operational memory: content\n  tied to a decision moment, a handoff between executions, or something\n  meant to be reviewed and eventually expire.\n- A durable fact or convention that will not become false and carries no\n  review trigger — a third-party tool's parsing quirk, a naming\n  convention, a recurring gotcha — is not a `decision-log` just because no\n  better type exists. Route it to `.pose/rules/` instead: add it to an\n  existing rule file or create one, then wire it into the relevant task\n  type's base `rules` array in `.pose/indexes/task-map.json` so\n  `pose suggest <task>` surfaces it automatically. No path scoping is\n  required — a task type's base `rules` list is returned regardless of\n  `--path`; only language/component-specific rules need the\n  `rules_by_domain` layer.\n- Rule of thumb: if nothing was decided or traded off, and nothing about\n  the fact will change on a predictable timeline, it is not a\n  `decision-log` and not an ADR — it is a rule. See ADR\n  `2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type`.\n\n## Reusable cross-execution format\n\n- Structure reusable context as a handoff with fixed sections: Context, Current state, Next checks, Risks, and Next owner.\n- Keep `source_refs` linked to the relevant spec, workflow, and executed check commands.\n- Record `last_reviewed_at` in the body to make effective cross-execution updates traceable.\n\n## Archiving and purging\n\n- Run biweekly triage to list expired artifacts.\n- Move expired artifacts to `.pose/knowledge/archive/` when they retain audit value.\n- Purge archived artifacts 180 days after expiration unless documented legal or compliance requirements apply.\n- Record every archive and purge action in the housekeeping log.\n\n## Sensitive content\n\n- Prohibit secrets, tokens, credentials, private keys, and equivalent material.\n- Prohibit personal data and non-anonymized customer data.\n- Do not copy restricted incidents or reports in full; keep only a controlled reference.\n- Classify frontmatter `sensitivity` as `public-internal` or `restricted`.\n- Remove identified sensitive content immediately and open a security follow-up.\n\n## Ownership and review\n\n- Keep `@pose-maintainers` as the primary governance owner.\n- Require an owner in every artifact frontmatter.\n- Review expiration biweekly and quality monthly.\n- Escalate a backlog overdue by more than two cycles to the primary owner.\n- Block backlog growth when `list-expired` exceeds the operational limit: zero in strict mode, two in tolerant mode.\n\n## Minimum operational checks\n\n- Run `pose knowledge-check --strict` biweekly to validate the expired backlog.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping list-expired` for detailed triage.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping archive-expired --dry-run` before applying changes.\n- Execute destructive actions only with an explicit `--apply` flag.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The focused tests cover ordinary commits, untracked files, and repeated edits to a dirty file. I’m checking whether the key also covers authorization, read-view snapshots, and paths Git reports only as directories. Those boundaries determine whether reuse is safe."}}
